<title>SOUTH AFRICA: Remgro lifts year earnings.</title>
<headline>Remgro lifts year earnings.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-06-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year ended March 31</p>
<p>			(million rand unless stated)</p>
<p>Shr, (cts)</p>
<p>    - pre-exceps	    371.1	 vs 283.9</p>
<p>    - post exceps	   422.6	 vs 283.7</p>
<p>Analysts polled by Reuters forecast earnings for the year to March 31 rising to between 327 cents and 380 cents, with consensus at 355.7 cents.</p>
<p>Remgro in February declared a dividend of 76.84 cents for the 12 month period compared with 62.45 the previous year.  </p>
<p>    Attrib income	   2,206	 vs 1,481</p>
<p>    Pre-tax		   433	   vs 943</p>
<p>    Tax			 150	   vs 331</p>
<p>    Interest paid	   107	   vs 163</p>
<p>Operating income before interest and depreciation</p>
<p>				  716	   vs 1,269</p>
<p>    Dividend income	 626	   vs 262</p>
<p>Equity adjustment, share of net income retained by associated firms</p>
<p>				  1,101	 vs 687</p>
<p>    Exceptional items     303	   vs nil</p>
<p>Full name: Rembrandt Group Ltd</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
</text>
